    [Doc][PCP] Separate graph and speculative compatibility (#18432)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The PCP support matrix now has a separate `Graph Mode + PCP` column.
    Each backend reports `Partial compatibility (FULL not supported)`
    directly in the Graph Mode + PCP column. The `Speculative Decoding +
    PCP` column lists only supported methods: MTP for MLA, MTP for SFA,
    Eagle3 for GQA, MTP and DSpark for DSA, and DSpark for DSA V4.1. SFA now
    explicitly includes DSpark.
    
    This addresses the documentation review in #17995:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/17995#discussion_r4236740066.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Documentation-only clarification; the supported combinations remain
    unchanged. This PR targets main only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Passed markdownlint-cli 0.45.0 with the repository configuration for
    the changed document.
    - Passed git diff --check.
    - bash format.sh ci was attempted but cannot run locally because
    pre-commit is unavailable. Full repository checks are left to CI.
    - No runtime tests are needed for this documentation-only change.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: t00911734 <tangdafu@huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: t00911734 <tangdafu@huawei.com>

